cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "本ソフトウェアを利用した場合は、以下を引用してください。 / If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software

title: "shoken-model: 全国471,024メッシュで測った店舗立地の予測可能性"

abstract: >-
  Fits Poisson location models for 30 retail, food-service and personal-service
  formats over all 471,024 inhabited 500 m mesh cells of Japan (125.3 million
  people), and validates them prospectively against 74,507 actual store openings
  drawn from three public licensing registries.

  Four principal results. (1) Ranking empty cells works: the top 10% of cells
  captured 75.1% of new convenience stores, a 7.5x lift (95% CI 7.3-7.7).
  (2) A single national model suffices; coefficients fitted on one prefecture
  transfer to the other 46 with a penalty of at most 0.031 AUC, even though
  individual coefficients vary threefold across prefectures. (3) The direction
  of the question matters: where a given format goes is predictable, but which
  format appears in a given cell is not (mean AUC 0.508), because population,
  employment, roads, stations and land use push every format the same way.
  (4) Daytime employment is the only feature that helps; age structure, land
  price, station ridership and building counts add nothing, and the latter two
  are absorbed by employment.

  Clustering is then decomposed. Chain agglomeration is dominant-strategy
  expansion — a chain's own local share discriminates its openings from rivals'
  at AUC 0.57-0.93 — while independent-store agglomeration repels chains and is
  not explained by terrain, history or zoning (at most 31% of the explainable
  residual, and mostly by neighbouring residuals rather than any site attribute).

  全国471,024メッシュ・30業種の立地を、公的な許認可3系統から集めた74,507件の
  実際の開店で前向きに検証した記録。まだ1店も無いマスの順位づけは7.5倍で当たり、
  全国1つのモデルで足りる。ただし「どこか」は当てられても「何の店か」は当てられない。
  効いた特徴量は従業者数だけで、集積の正体はドミナント出店だった。

